fix: open the browser only when the web client is fully ready

The launcher polled GET / (the shell answers 200 as soon as the HTTP server
binds), so the browser often opened before the host's connection layer was
registered — the page then booted to "Failed to load plugins" with every
entry pending on `connection` (a refresh recovered it).

Readiness now requires the shell AND the client API transport: GET
/api/events.mux must answer 426 Upgrade Required (the connection plugin's
route), which is what every client plugin depends on.

- probe.ts: new probeApiReady (GET /api/events.mux == 426)
- webui.ts: status()/start() consider the app ready only when both probes
  pass; webui_start waits for the API transport instead of the bare shell
- desktop.ts: launch.cmd polls both endpoints via curl.exe (%% is cmd's
  literal-percent escape for %{http_code}); launch.sh gains an is_ready()
  helper with the same check

Verified against the live harness: GET / = 200, GET /api/events.mux = 426;
34 tests pass (new API-transport gating test).
